# Pinned source of the NFSv3 XDR in this directory.
#
# RFC 1813 prints no extraction script: its XDR is spread through the prose,
# one definition per section.  nfs3.x is assembled from the pinned text by
# ../rfc_xdr.py, one `copy` or `constant` line per definition below, in the
# RFC's own order; nothing in it is written by hand.  ../README.md describes
# the rules; the directives are documented at the top of ../rfc_xdr.py.
#
#   rfc_xdr.py SOURCES --check     nfs3.x matches its pin (build.sh)
#   rfc_xdr.py SOURCES --verify    fetch the RFC and rebuild nfs3.x
#
# Errata: RFC 1813 has none (errata.rfc-editor.org, 2026-10-16).
#
# Only the NFS program (100003, version 3) is taken.  The MOUNT and NLM
# protocols of RFC 1813's appendices run on their own programs and ports,
# and NFSACL (100227), which shares port 2049 with NFSv3 on Linux, is in no
# RFC; all three stay unsupported_schema.

rfc 1813 55118e8a8c2ee6031bede635c6d5beba10ef21fe7d23837c7145ca9c85905b20

assemble nfs3.x 29d3f018c9fd05207969ebd22c6ccb2a1e11576c3b24f3333af84d512b407d95

# Section 2.4: the sizes, stated as prose.
constant 1813 NFS3_FHSIZE
constant 1813 NFS3_COOKIEVERFSIZE
constant 1813 NFS3_CREATEVERFSIZE
constant 1813 NFS3_WRITEVERFSIZE

# Sections 2.5 and 2.6: basic data types and structures.  uint32 and int32
# are `unsigned long` and `long`, which normalize.py reads as rpcgen does:
